          Eucalyptus oil is dominated by <strong>1,8-cineole</strong>, an active compound studied for over forty years. A 2010 review in <em>Alternative Medicine Review</em> documented its inhalation safety profile and respiratory action at therapeutic doses. In Lio it serves a sensory role — the cool, open feeling on the inhale — at concentrations far below therapeutic levels.
