      <ul class="lsv2-compare-flow">
        <li><span class="step">1</span> Battery powers heating coil</li>
        <li><span class="step">2</span> Coil heats e-liquid to 200–300°C</li>
        <li><span class="step">3</span> Liquid aerosolizes into vapor</li>
        <li><span class="step">4</span> User inhales aerosol particles</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="lsv2-compare-output">
        <strong>What enters the lungs:</strong> aerosolized propylene glycol, glycerin, nicotine (in most), flavorant compounds heated past their food-safety profile. <button class="lsv2-ref" data-ref="13">13</button><button class="lsv2-ref" data-ref="14">14</button>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="lsv2-compare-col is-lio lsv2-reveal">
      <div class="lsv2-compare-col-head"><span class="marker"></span> Lio</div>
      <h3>Passes air across a fiber matrix</h3>

      <div class="lsv2-compare-diagram" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="lsv2-lio-device"></div>
        <div class="lsv2-lio-airflow"></div>
        <div class="lsv2-lio-airflow"></div>
        <div class="lsv2-lio-airflow"></div>
        <div class="lsv2-lio-airflow"></div>
        <div class="lsv2-lio-airflow"></div>
        <div class="lsv2-lio-aroma"></div>
        <div class="lsv2-lio-aroma"></div>
        <div class="lsv2-lio-aroma"></div>
        <div class="lsv2-compare-diagram-label">Ambient temp · airflow only</div>
      </div>

      <ul class="lsv2-compare-flow">
        <li><span class="step">1</span> User inhales through wooden barrel</li>
        <li><span class="step">2</span> Air flows across oil-infused core</li>
        <li><span class="step">3</span> Air picks up aromatic molecules</li>
        <li><span class="step">4</span> Scent travels on user's own breath</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="lsv2-compare-output">
        <strong>What enters the lungs:</strong> ambient air carrying the same volatile aromatic molecules diffused in any aromatherapy room. No combustion, no aerosolization, no exhaled cloud.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="lsv2-compare-disclaimer lsv2-reveal">
    <strong>One honest caveat.</strong> The long-term safety of essential-oil inhalation is not as exhaustively studied as inhalation pharmaceuticals. Lio's compounds have a long history of safe use in aromatherapy and food. If you have asthma, COPD, or any respiratory condition, talk with your doctor before starting. We'd rather lose the sale than cause an issue.
