<!-- 8. HONESTY -->
<section class="lsv2-honesty" id="lsv2-honesty">
  <div class="lsv2-honesty-inner">

    <div class="lsv2-honesty-head lsv2-reveal">
      <div class="lsv2-eyebrow dark">What the evidence does not say</div>
      <h2 class="lsv2-h-section">Things <span class="lsv2-italic">we will not claim.</span></h2>
      <p class="lsv2-lede dark">A healthy skepticism is the right posture toward any wellness product. Above is what the literature supports. Here is the equally important other half.</p>
    </div>

    <ol class="lsv2-honesty-list">

      <li class="lsv2-honesty-item lsv2-reveal">
        <div>
          <h3>Lio is not a smoking-cessation drug.</h3>
          <p>It has not been submitted to or approved by the FDA, EMA, or any equivalent body as a cessation aid. The studies we cite describe ingredient effects, not regulatory clearance for the Lio device itself. Lio is registered and marketed in the EU as a wellness and aromatherapy device.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="lsv2-honesty-item lsv2-reveal">
        <div>
          <h3>The studies we cite are <span class="lsv2-italic">small.</span></h3>
          <p>The foundational Rose &amp; Behm trial had 48 participants. The 2013 Cordell &amp; Buckle study had 20. These are pilot-scale, not phase-3. The effect direction is consistent across thirty years of independent replications, but absolute effect sizes are modest.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="lsv2-honesty-item lsv2-reveal">
        <div>
          <h3>It will not work for everyone.</h3>
          <p>Habits run on many circuits — sensory, social, emotional, chemical. Lio addresses the sensorimotor-and-scent layer well. Heavy chemical dependence, severe psychological distress, or social-context triggers may need professional support. Our 30-day return policy exists precisely because we know it doesn't land for everyone.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="lsv2-honesty-item lsv2-reveal">
        <div>
          <h3>The 82% craving figure is <span class="lsv2-italic">our own data.</span></h3>
          <p>It is a self-reported user survey (n = 1,243, 2024), not a randomized clinical trial. It is meaningful as customer experience, not as clinical evidence. We label it as such everywhere it appears.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="lsv2-honesty-item lsv2-reveal">
        <div>
          <h3>Long-term inhalation data is incomplete.</h3>
          <p>The mechanism — passive air over an oil-infused fiber — has decades of analogous use in commercial aromatherapy. But specific multi-year inhalation studies on this exact format do not exist. We are honest about this. If it matters to you, the responsible move is to talk to your doctor.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

    </ol>

  </div>
</section>


